//@version=6
// =============================================================================
// XAUUSD Disciplined Agent -- chart-native version
// =============================================================================
// Draws every signal on the chart with its SL, TP1 and TP2, for live bars and
// for all history, and reports real statistics in TradingView's Strategy Tester.
//
// HOW TO USE
//   1. Open CAPITALCOM:XAUUSD (the feed this account already charts).
//      Timeframe: 15m or 1h. The chart timeframe supplies BOTH the
//      order-block zone and the entry trigger, so it is the zone timeframe of
//      the design. On 5m the zones are 5-minute zones -- far noisier, and a
//      60-bar zone lifetime is only 5 hours. 1h is the designed setting; 15m
//      is a reasonable intraday compromise.
//   2. Pine Editor -> paste this -> Save -> Add to chart.
//   3. Set "Bias timeframe" to 4h (or 1D for a slower, more selective read).
//   4. Open the Strategy Tester tab for win rate, profit factor and drawdown,
//      and "List of Trades" for every historical entry with its exit.
//
// TIMEFRAME LAYOUT -- READ THIS
//   The Python engine uses three timeframes (15m entry / 1h zone / 4h bias).
//   This script uses two: the CHART timeframe supplies both the order-block
//   zone and the Heikin Ashi entry trigger, and one higher timeframe supplies
//   the bias. The reason is non-repainting: order-block state is a running
//   value, and pulling a running value off a third timeframe through
//   request.security cannot be made reliably non-repainting. Two timeframes
//   can. So run this on 1h, which is the zone timeframe of the Python design.
//
//   Consequence: this script and the Python engine will not agree trade for
//   trade. The Python engine remains the source of truth for the journal and
//   the promotion gate. This script is for seeing the logic on a chart and for
//   a fast, independent check of the edge using TradingView's own tester.
//
// NON-REPAINTING
//   The bias uses request.security(..., f()[1], lookahead_on), the canonical
//   non-repainting idiom: it returns the last CLOSED higher-timeframe bar,
//   which is what the Python align_index() does. Entries are evaluated on bar
//   close (process_orders_on_close). Historical and live behaviour match.
//
// CHECK YOU ARE RUNNING THIS BUILD
//   The chart legend must read "XAU Agent v5 ...". If it reads "XAU Agent"
//   with no version, the chart is still running an older copy and none of the
//   fixes below are active -- pasting into the Pine Editor does not update an
//   instance that is already on the chart unless you save the SAME script.
//   Remove the indicator from the chart, then Save and Add to chart again.
//
// IF YOU SEE NO TRADES
//   Open the status panel (top right). It counts every bar against the FIRST
//   gate it failed, so the largest number names the binding constraint. Two
//   gates were measured to be the usual culprits, and both now have safer
//   defaults: the bias rule (strict structure gives a usable bias on only
//   45.5% of real 4h gold bars, the EMA fallback gives 69.7%) and the
//   volatility gate (which used to be an absolute ATR-percent band and
//   rejected every single 5m bar).
//
// FEED MATTERS
//   Volume conventions differ by provider, and the displacement volume filter
//   is calibrated against real data. Measured on gold 1h:
//       OANDA       volume ratio p90 1.90, max 6.53, 20.6% clear 1.4x
//       CAPITALCOM  volume ratio p90 1.54, max 2.14, 16.7% clear 1.4x
//   Both work at 1.4. But CAPITALCOM volume is less spiky, so do NOT raise the
//   volume threshold above about 1.8 on it -- only 2.5% of bars clear that, and
//   above 2.5 literally none do, which silences the script completely.
//
// WHAT IT CANNOT DO
//   Pine cannot place orders with your broker. This draws and measures.
// =============================================================================

// Notes on the settings below -- these MUST stay outside the call.
//
//   Pine does not allow a comment line inside a multi-line function call. The
//   comment terminates the call, so the remaining arguments are orphaned and
//   the whole script mis-parses. The symptom is misleading: the compiler then
//   reports CE10244 ("a strategy must contain at least one ... plot")
//   against line 1, even though the script is full of plots and orders.
//
//   slippage = 25
//     25 ticks at a 0.01 mintick is $0.25, a realistic XAUUSD spread, and the
//     same cost the Python backtester charges. Without it the tester reports
//     meaningfully better numbers than you would actually be filled at.
//
//   process_orders_on_close = true
//     Orders fill at the close of the signal bar. The Python engine is one
//     notch more conservative -- it fills at the NEXT bar's open -- so expect
//     this tester to read slightly better than the Python backtest.

strategy("XAUUSD Disciplined Agent", shorttitle = "XAU Agent v5", overlay = true, initial_capital = 50000, currency = currency.USD, default_qty_type = strategy.fixed, default_qty_value = 1, commission_type = strategy.commission.cash_per_contract, commission_value = 0.0, slippage = 25, process_orders_on_close = true, calc_on_every_tick = false, max_boxes_count = 500, max_labels_count = 500, max_lines_count = 500)

// A global output, declared immediately after the strategy() call so it cannot
// be affected by anything later in the script. Value is na, so it draws
// nothing; it exists to guarantee the CE10244 output requirement is met.
plot(na, "anchor")

// ----------------------------------------------------------------- inputs

grpR = "Risk (hard limits)"
acctEquity   = input.float(50000.0, "Account equity ($)",      group=grpR, minval=100)
riskPct = input.float(0.5, "Risk per trade (%)", group=grpR, minval=0.05, maxval=1.0, step=0.05, tooltip="Capped at 1%. 0.5% of $50,000 = $250, so one 2R winner meets a $500 day.")
dailyTarget = input.float(500.0, "Daily profit target ($)", group=grpR, minval=0, tooltip="Reaching it stops trading for the day. Giving profit back is a real failure mode.")
dailyMaxLoss = input.float(500.0,   "Daily loss cap ($)",      group=grpR, minval=0)
maxTrades    = input.int(3,         "Max trades per day",      group=grpR, minval=1, maxval=10)
maxConsecL   = input.int(2,         "Consecutive losses then stop", group=grpR, minval=1, maxval=5)
cooloffMin = input.int(30, "Cool-off after a loss (min)", group=grpR, minval=0, tooltip="The anti-revenge rule. No new entry inside this window.")
minRR        = input.float(1.8,     "Minimum reward:risk",     group=grpR, minval=1.0, step=0.1)

grpB = "Bias"
biasTF = input.timeframe("240", "Bias timeframe", group=grpB, tooltip="240 = 4h. Use 1D for a slower, more selective read.")
emaFast  = input.int(50,  "Fast EMA", group=grpB, minval=5)
emaSlow  = input.int(200, "Slow EMA", group=grpB, minval=20)
swingLB  = input.int(2,   "Swing fractal strength", group=grpB, minval=1, maxval=10)
biasMode = input.string("ema_fallback", "Bias rule", options=["strict", "ema_fallback"], group=grpB)

grpZ = "Order blocks"
atrLen      = input.int(14,   "ATR length",                group=grpZ, minval=2)
dispATR = input.float(1.3,"Displacement (x ATR)", group=grpZ, minval=0.3, step=0.1, tooltip="Body of the impulse candle as a multiple of ATR. On real gold 1h, 3.6% of bars clear 1.3.")
minVolRatio = input.float(1.4,"Displacement volume (x avg)",group=grpZ, minval=0.5, step=0.1, tooltip="Volume on the DISPLACEMENT candle, not the block candle. Measured on 400 real gold 1h bars, displacement candles run a median 1.83x average while block candles run 0.84x -- putting this filter on the block candle rejects nearly every genuine setup.")
volLB       = input.int(20,   "Volume average length",     group=grpZ, minval=5)
obMaxAge    = input.int(60,   "Zone max age (bars)",       group=grpZ, minval=5)
tapTolATR   = input.float(0.35,"Tap tolerance (x ATR)",    group=grpZ, minval=0.0, step=0.05)
obSearchBack= input.int(20,   "Look back for block candle",group=grpZ, minval=3, maxval=50)
tapGrace    = input.int(6,    "Tap stays live for (bars)", group=grpZ, minval=1, maxval=30)

grpT = "Trigger and targets"
haConfirm   = input.int(2,    "Heikin Ashi confirm bars",  group=grpT, minval=1, maxval=5)
haMaxWick = input.float(0.62,"Max HA wick ratio", group=grpT, minval=0.1, maxval=0.95, step=0.01, tooltip="1.0 is a pure doji. Above this the candle is indecision, not a turn.")
minScore = input.int(70, "Minimum confluence score", group=grpT, minval=0, maxval=100, tooltip="The primary overtrading control. Raise for fewer, better trades.")
slBufATR    = input.float(0.55,"SL buffer (x ATR)",        group=grpT, minval=0.0, step=0.05)
slSwingLB   = input.int(12,   "SL swing lookback",         group=grpT, minval=3)
tp1R        = input.float(1.0, "TP1 (R)",                  group=grpT, minval=0.3, step=0.1)
tp1Pct      = input.int(50,   "Close at TP1 (%)",          group=grpT, minval=10, maxval=90)
tp2R        = input.float(2.2, "TP2 (R)",                  group=grpT, minval=0.5, step=0.1)
beAtTP1     = input.bool(true,"Move SL to breakeven at TP1", group=grpT)

grpS = "Sessions and volatility"
// Volatility is measured RELATIVE to the instrument's own recent average, not
// as an absolute percentage of price. An absolute band is timeframe-dependent
// and silently breaks the script: gold's ATR is about 0.38% of price on 1h but
// only ~0.11% on 5m, so the old 0.12% floor rejected every single 5m bar and
// the strategy produced no trades at all on that timeframe. A ratio to the
// 100-bar average ATR means the same settings work on 5m, 15m and 1h.
volAvgLen   = input.int(100,  "Volatility baseline (bars)", group=grpS, minval=20)
minVolMult  = input.float(0.55,"Min volatility (x own average)", group=grpS, minval=0.1, step=0.05)
maxVolMult  = input.float(2.50,"Max volatility (x own average)", group=grpS, minval=0.5, step=0.1)
asianPenalty= input.int(12, "Asian session penalty", group=grpS, minval=0, maxval=40, tooltip="Gold produces its most false breaks 00:00-07:00 UTC. Penalised, not banned.")

grpV = "Display"
showZones   = input.bool(true, "Draw order-block zones",   group=grpV)
showTrades  = input.bool(true, "Draw SL / TP boxes",       group=grpV)
showLabels  = input.bool(true, "Label entries with score", group=grpV)
showTable   = input.bool(true, "Show status panel",        group=grpV)
colLong     = input.color(color.new(#26a69a, 0), "Long",   group=grpV)
colShort    = input.color(color.new(#ef5350, 0), "Short",  group=grpV)
colSL       = input.color(color.new(#ef5350, 78), "SL fill", group=grpV)
colTP       = input.color(color.new(#26a69a, 78), "TP fill", group=grpV)

riskUSD = acctEquity * math.min(riskPct, 1.0) / 100.0

// ------------------------------------------------------- chart-TF indicators

atrv   = ta.atr(atrLen)
volAvg = ta.sma(volume, volLB)
volRat = volAvg > 0 ? volume / volAvg : na

// Heikin Ashi, taken from the HA ticker so it matches what TradingView draws.
// HA is the TRIGGER only. Every price level below comes from real OHLC --
// HA open/close are synthetic averages and are not tradeable prices.
haT   = ticker.heikinashi(syminfo.tickerid)
haO   = request.security(haT, timeframe.period, open,  lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_off)
haC   = request.security(haT, timeframe.period, close, lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_off)
haH   = request.security(haT, timeframe.period, high,  lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_off)
haL   = request.security(haT, timeframe.period, low,   lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_off)

haBull    = haC >= haO
haRange   = haH - haL
haWickRat = haRange > 0 ? 1.0 - (math.abs(haC - haO) / haRange) : 1.0

// --------------------------------------------------------------- HTF bias
// Returns 1 bull, -1 bear, 0 stand aside. Structure decides; the EMAs veto.
f_bias() =>
    ph = ta.pivothigh(high, swingLB, swingLB)
    pl = ta.pivotlow(low,  swingLB, swingLB)
    var float h1 = na
    var float h2 = na
    var float l1 = na
    var float l2 = na
    if not na(ph)
        h2 := h1
        h1 := ph
    if not na(pl)
        l2 := l1
        l1 := pl
    ef = ta.ema(close, emaFast)
    es = ta.ema(close, emaSlow)
    ready = not na(h1) and not na(h2) and not na(l1) and not na(l2)
    bull  = ready and h1 > h2 and l1 > l2      // higher high + higher low
    bear  = ready and h1 < h2 and l1 < l2      // lower high + lower low
    int b = 0
    if bull and not na(ef) and not na(es) and close >= math.min(ef, es)
        b := 1
    else if bear and not na(ef) and not na(es) and close <= math.max(ef, es)
        b := -1
    // Structure had no opinion: fall back to the EMA trend. Measured over 69
    // days of real 4h gold, strict structure gave a usable bias on only 45.5%
    // of bars; with this fallback it is 69.7%. Bias is a mandatory gate, so
    // that difference alone decides whether the strategy ever trades.
    if b == 0 and biasMode == "ema_fallback" and not na(ef) and not na(es)
        if close > ef and ef > es
            b := 1
        else if close < ef and ef < es
            b := -1
    b

// f()[1] with lookahead_on is the canonical non-repainting pattern: it yields
// the last CLOSED higher-timeframe bar on both history and realtime.
biasHTF = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, biasTF, f_bias()[1], lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_on)
bias    = nz(biasHTF, 0)

// ------------------------------------------------------- order block tracking
// A displacement candle (big body AND heavy volume) qualifies the last
// opposing candle before it as a zone. The zone dies when price CLOSES through
// it -- a mere touch is the entry trigger we are waiting for, not invalidation.
var float dTop  = na   // demand (long) zone
var float dBot  = na
var int   dBar  = na
var float dDisp = na
var float dVol  = na

var float sTop  = na   // supply (short) zone
var float sBot  = na
var int   sBar  = na
var float sDisp = na
var float sVol  = na

bodySize = math.abs(close - open)
isDisp   = not na(atrv) and atrv > 0 and not na(volRat) and
           bodySize >= dispATR * atrv and volRat >= minVolRatio
bullDisp = isDisp and close > open
bearDisp = isDisp and close < open

if bullDisp
    for i = 1 to obSearchBack
        if close[i] < open[i]              // last bearish candle before the push
            dTop  := high[i]
            dBot  := low[i]
            dBar  := bar_index - i
            dDisp := bodySize / atrv
            dVol  := volRat
            break

if bearDisp
    for i = 1 to obSearchBack
        if close[i] > open[i]              // last bullish candle before the drop
            sTop  := high[i]
            sBot  := low[i]
            sBar  := bar_index - i
            sDisp := bodySize / atrv
            sVol  := volRat
            break

// Invalidate on a close through the far edge, and expire on age.
if not na(dBot) and (close < dBot or bar_index - dBar > obMaxAge)
    dTop := na
    dBot := na
if not na(sTop) and (close > sTop or bar_index - sBar > obMaxAge)
    sTop := na
    sBot := na

// Draw the live zones once, when they form.
if showZones and bullDisp and not na(dBot)
    box.new(dBar, dTop, bar_index + 8, dBot, border_color = color.new(colLong, 35), bgcolor = color.new(colLong, 88))
if showZones and bearDisp and not na(sTop)
    box.new(sBar, sTop, bar_index + 8, sBot, border_color = color.new(colShort, 35), bgcolor = color.new(colShort, 88))

// --------------------------------------------------------------- session

hourUTC  = hour(time, "UTC")
isAsian  = hourUTC >= 0  and hourUTC < 7
isLondon = hourUTC >= 7  and hourUTC < 13
isNY     = hourUTC >= 13 and hourUTC < 21
sessName = isNY ? "newyork" : isLondon ? "london" : isAsian ? "asian" : "offhours"

// ------------------------------------------------------------- daily state

var float dayPnl      = 0.0
var int   tradesToday = 0
var int   consecLoss  = 0
var int   lastLossT   = na
var int   seenClosed  = 0

newDay = ta.change(time("D")) != 0
if newDay
    dayPnl      := 0.0
    tradesToday := 0
    consecLoss  := 0
    lastLossT   := na

// Absorb newly closed trades into the daily counters.
if strategy.closedtrades > seenClosed
    for i = seenClosed to strategy.closedtrades - 1
        p = strategy.closedtrades.profit(i)
        dayPnl := dayPnl + p
        if p < 0
            consecLoss := consecLoss + 1
            lastLossT  := time
        else if p > 0
            consecLoss := 0
    seenClosed := strategy.closedtrades

coolOffActive = not na(lastLossT) and (time - lastLossT) < cooloffMin * 60 * 1000

// ------------------------------------------------------------- scoring

atrAvg  = ta.sma(atrv, volAvgLen)
volMult = not na(atrAvg) and atrAvg > 0 ? atrv / atrAvg : na
volOK   = not na(volMult) and volMult >= minVolMult and volMult <= maxVolMult

wantLong  = bias ==  1
wantShort = bias == -1

// Heikin Ashi trigger: N clean candles our way, none mostly wick, and we
// prefer a fresh flip over joining a mature run.
haAllLong  = true
haAllShort = true
haWorstWick = 0.0
for i = 0 to haConfirm - 1
    haAllLong  := haAllLong  and haBull[i]
    haAllShort := haAllShort and not haBull[i]
    haWorstWick := math.max(haWorstWick, nz(haWickRat[i], 1.0))

haWickOK   = haWorstWick <= haMaxWick
haFlipLong  = haAllLong  and not haBull[haConfirm]
haFlipShort = haAllShort and haBull[haConfirm]
haLongOK   = haAllLong  and haWickOK
haShortOK  = haAllShort and haWickOK

// Zone proximity. "At" includes trading inside the zone -- that IS the tap.
tapTol = tapTolATR * nz(atrv, 0.0)

longZoneReady  = wantLong  and not na(dBot) and dBot <= close
shortZoneReady = wantShort and not na(sTop) and sTop >= close

// A tap counts if it happened on this bar or within the grace window. The
// trade is "price reached the zone, then turned", and the turn is allowed to
// take a few bars -- demanding the tap and the Heikin Ashi flip on the same
// bar is not how the setup is actually traded.
longTapRaw  = longZoneReady  and low  <= dTop + tapTol
shortTapRaw = shortZoneReady and high >= sBot - tapTol
longTapped  = longZoneReady  and nz(ta.barssince(longTapRaw),  9999) < tapGrace
shortTapped = shortZoneReady and nz(ta.barssince(shortTapRaw), 9999) < tapGrace

longDist  = longZoneReady  and atrv > 0 ? math.abs(close - (dTop + dBot) / 2) / atrv : na
shortDist = shortZoneReady and atrv > 0 ? math.abs(close - (sTop + sBot) / 2) / atrv : na

// RSI is computed once at global scope. Calling ta.rsi() inside f_score would
// create a separate series per call site, which is both wasteful and a common
// source of subtle Pine bugs.
rsiV = ta.rsi(close, 14)

// Scoring mirrors the Python engine with one documented difference: Python
// awards 25 for bias when the last structural event was a clean break of
// structure and 18 otherwise. This script does not track BOS/CHoCH separately,
// so it always awards the conservative 18. The practical effect is that the
// maximum reachable score here is 93, not 100, which makes any given threshold
// slightly STRICTER than the same number in Python. That is the safe direction.
// Parameters are deliberately untyped: Pine user-function signatures do not
// take type annotations, and adding them is a compile error.
f_score(isLong, tapped, dist, disp, vr, flip) =>
    int sc = 0
    // HTF bias: 18 of a possible 25 (mandatory -- no bias means no trade)
    sc := sc + 18
    // Order block quality: 20
    sc := sc + 10
    if not na(disp) and disp >= dispATR * 1.5
        sc := sc + 5
    if not na(vr) and vr >= minVolRatio * 1.4
        sc := sc + 5
    // At the zone: 15
    if tapped
        sc := sc + 15
    else if not na(dist) and dist <= 2.0
        sc := sc + 7
    // HA trigger: 15 (mandatory)
    sc := sc + (flip ? 15 : 9)
    // Entry volume: 10
    if not na(volRat) and volRat >= 1.2
        sc := sc + 10
    else if not na(volRat) and volRat >= 0.9
        sc := sc + 5
    // Volatility regime: 10
    if volOK
        sc := sc + 10
    // Momentum not exhausted: 5
    if not na(rsiV) and ((isLong and rsiV < 68) or (not isLong and rsiV > 32))
        sc := sc + 5
    // Session penalty
    if isAsian
        sc := sc - asianPenalty
    math.max(0, math.min(100, sc))

longScore  = f_score(true,  longTapped,  longDist,  dDisp, dVol, haFlipLong)
shortScore = f_score(false, shortTapped, shortDist, sDisp, sVol, haFlipShort)

// ------------------------------------------------------------- trade plan

swingLow  = ta.lowest(low,   slSwingLB)
swingHigh = ta.highest(high, slSwingLB)

longEntry = close
longSL    = math.min(swingLow, nz(dBot, swingLow)) - slBufATR * nz(atrv, 0)
longRisk  = longEntry - longSL
longTP1   = longEntry + tp1R * longRisk
longTP2   = longEntry + tp2R * longRisk

shortEntry = close
shortSL    = math.max(swingHigh, nz(sTop, swingHigh)) + slBufATR * nz(atrv, 0)
shortRisk  = shortSL - shortEntry
shortTP1   = shortEntry - tp1R * shortRisk
shortTP2   = shortEntry - tp2R * shortRisk

longRR  = longRisk  > 0 ? (longTP2  - longEntry) / longRisk  : 0.0
shortRR = shortRisk > 0 ? (shortEntry - shortTP2) / shortRisk : 0.0

// ------------------------------------------------------------- risk gate

flat          = strategy.position_size == 0
targetMet     = dailyTarget  > 0 and dayPnl >=  dailyTarget
lossCapHit    = dailyMaxLoss > 0 and dayPnl <= -dailyMaxLoss
tradeCapHit   = tradesToday >= maxTrades
lossStreakHit = consecLoss  >= maxConsecL

riskOK = flat and not targetMet and not lossCapHit and not tradeCapHit and
         not lossStreakHit and not coolOffActive and barstate.isconfirmed

longSignal  = riskOK and wantLong  and longZoneReady  and longTapped  and
              haLongOK  and volOK and longScore  >= minScore and
              longRisk  > 0 and longRR  >= minRR
shortSignal = riskOK and wantShort and shortZoneReady and shortTapped and
              haShortOK and volOK and shortScore >= minScore and
              shortRisk > 0 and shortRR >= minRR

// Ounces such that a stop-out loses exactly the risk budget. NOTE: on most
// XAUUSD feeds 1 contract = 1 ounce and a $1 move is $1 per contract, so this
// is the right unit -- but verify against your broker before sizing live.
longQty  = longRisk  > 0 ? math.max(1, math.floor(riskUSD / longRisk))  : 1
shortQty = shortRisk > 0 ? math.max(1, math.floor(riskUSD / shortRisk)) : 1

// ------------------------------------------------------------- execution

var float pendSL  = na
var float pendTP1 = na
var float pendTP2 = na
var float pendEnt = na
var int   pendDir = 0
var int   pendBar = na
var int   pendScore = 0

if longSignal
    strategy.entry("Long", strategy.long, qty=longQty, comment="L " + str.tostring(longScore))
    pendSL    := longSL
    pendTP1   := longTP1
    pendTP2   := longTP2
    pendEnt   := longEntry
    pendDir   := 1
    pendBar   := bar_index
    pendScore := longScore
    tradesToday := tradesToday + 1

if shortSignal
    strategy.entry("Short", strategy.short, qty=shortQty, comment="S " + str.tostring(shortScore))
    pendSL    := shortSL
    pendTP1   := shortTP1
    pendTP2   := shortTP2
    pendEnt   := shortEntry
    pendDir   := -1
    pendBar   := bar_index
    pendScore := shortScore
    tradesToday := tradesToday + 1

// Exits: half off at TP1, remainder at TP2, stop to breakeven after TP1.
// activeSL is hoisted to global scope so the plot section below can show the
// stop that is actually working, including after it moves to breakeven.
var bool  tp1Done  = false
var float activeSL = na
if strategy.position_size == 0
    tp1Done  := false
    activeSL := na

if strategy.position_size > 0
    activeSL := tp1Done and beAtTP1 ? pendEnt : pendSL
    // Exit ids are per-direction. Reusing one id across two different
    // from_entry values makes the order book ambiguous.
    strategy.exit("L-TP1", from_entry="Long", qty_percent=tp1Pct, limit=pendTP1, stop=activeSL, comment_profit="TP1", comment_loss="SL")
    strategy.exit("L-TP2", from_entry="Long", limit=pendTP2, stop=activeSL, comment_profit="TP2", comment_loss="SL")
    if high >= pendTP1
        tp1Done := true

if strategy.position_size < 0
    activeSL := tp1Done and beAtTP1 ? pendEnt : pendSL
    strategy.exit("S-TP1", from_entry="Short", qty_percent=tp1Pct, limit=pendTP1, stop=activeSL, comment_profit="TP1", comment_loss="SL")
    strategy.exit("S-TP2", from_entry="Short", limit=pendTP2, stop=activeSL, comment_profit="TP2", comment_loss="SL")
    if low <= pendTP1
        tp1Done := true

// --------------------------------------------------- draw the trade on entry

if showTrades and (longSignal or shortSignal)
    dir  = longSignal ? 1 : -1
    ent  = longSignal ? longEntry : shortEntry
    sl   = longSignal ? longSL    : shortSL
    t1   = longSignal ? longTP1   : shortTP1
    t2   = longSignal ? longTP2   : shortTP2
    rgt  = bar_index + 30
    // box.new takes (top, bottom) in that order, and for a short the stop sits
    // ABOVE the entry while TP2 sits below -- so the pairs must be ordered by
    // max/min rather than by role, or the boxes come out inverted on shorts.
    box.new(bar_index, math.max(ent, sl), rgt, math.min(ent, sl), border_color=color.new(colShort, 45), bgcolor=colSL, border_width=1)
    box.new(bar_index, math.max(ent, t2), rgt, math.min(ent, t2), border_color=color.new(colLong, 45), bgcolor=colTP, border_width=1)
    // TP1 partial line.
    line.new(bar_index, t1, rgt, t1, color=color.new(colLong, 25), style=line.style_dashed, width=1)
    // Entry line.
    line.new(bar_index, ent, rgt, ent, color=dir == 1 ? colLong : colShort, width=2)

if showLabels and (longSignal or shortSignal)
    dir   = longSignal ? 1 : -1
    sc    = longSignal ? longScore : shortScore
    ent   = longSignal ? longEntry : shortEntry
    sl    = longSignal ? longSL    : shortSL
    t2    = longSignal ? longTP2   : shortTP2
    rr    = longSignal ? longRR    : shortRR
    qty   = longSignal ? longQty   : shortQty
    txt   = (dir == 1 ? "LONG " : "SHORT ") + str.tostring(sc) + "/100" +
            "\nentry " + str.tostring(ent, format.mintick) +
            "\nSL "    + str.tostring(sl,  format.mintick) +
            "\nTP2 "   + str.tostring(t2,  format.mintick) +
            "\nR:R "   + str.tostring(rr, "#.##") +
            "\n"       + str.tostring(qty) + " oz  risk $" +
                         str.tostring(riskUSD, "#") +
            "\n"       + sessName
    label.new(bar_index, dir == 1 ? low : high, txt, style = dir == 1 ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down, color = color.new(dir == 1 ? colLong : colShort, 12), textcolor = color.white, size = size.small)

// --------------------------------------------------------- diagnostics
// An empty Strategy Tester is uninformative on its own: it cannot distinguish
// "the market never offered this setup" from "a filter is misconfigured and
// rejects everything". These counters classify each confirmed bar by the FIRST
// gate it failed, so the panel names the binding constraint.

var int nBias  = 0
var int nZone  = 0
var int nSide  = 0
var int nTap   = 0
var int nHA    = 0
var int nVol   = 0
var int nScore = 0
var int nRisk  = 0
var int nFired = 0
var int nBars  = 0

wantLongNow  = bias == 1
zoneExists   = wantLongNow ? not na(dBot) : not na(sTop)
zoneReadyNow = wantLongNow ? longZoneReady : shortZoneReady
tappedNow    = wantLongNow ? longTapped    : shortTapped
haOKNow      = wantLongNow ? haLongOK      : haShortOK
scoreNow     = wantLongNow ? longScore     : shortScore

if barstate.isconfirmed
    nBars := nBars + 1
    if bias == 0
        nBias := nBias + 1
    else if not zoneExists
        nZone := nZone + 1
    else if not zoneReadyNow
        nSide := nSide + 1
    else if not tappedNow
        nTap := nTap + 1
    else if not haOKNow
        nHA := nHA + 1
    else if not volOK
        nVol := nVol + 1
    else if scoreNow < minScore
        nScore := nScore + 1
    else if not riskOK
        nRisk := nRisk + 1
    else
        nFired := nFired + 1

f_pct(n) =>
    nBars > 0 ? str.tostring(n * 100.0 / nBars, "#.#") + "%" : "-"

// ------------------------------------------------------- plotted levels
// These plot() calls are REQUIRED, not decorative.
//
// Pine rejects a script with error CE10244 -- "a strategy must contain at least
// one of the following..." -- unless it has an output at GLOBAL scope. Every
// box.new, label.new and strategy.entry above sits inside an `if`, which is
// local scope, and a `var table t = table.new(...)` initialiser does not count
// either. So without at least one unconditional plot() the script will not
// compile, however much drawing it does.
//
// A plot cannot be wrapped in `if`, so visibility is controlled by feeding na
// into the value and using style_linebr, which breaks the line on na instead of
// interpolating across the gap.

plot(showZones ? dTop : na, "Demand zone top", color=color.new(colLong, 30), style=plot.style_linebr, linewidth=1)
plot(showZones ? dBot : na, "Demand zone bottom", color=color.new(colLong, 30), style=plot.style_linebr, linewidth=1)
plot(showZones ? sTop : na, "Supply zone top", color=color.new(colShort, 30), style=plot.style_linebr, linewidth=1)
plot(showZones ? sBot : na, "Supply zone bottom", color=color.new(colShort, 30), style=plot.style_linebr, linewidth=1)

// The live trade's working levels, so they stay visible after the entry boxes
// scroll away.
inPos = strategy.position_size != 0
plot(inPos ? pendEnt : na, "Active entry", color=color.new(color.white, 20), style=plot.style_linebr, linewidth=2)
plot(inPos ? activeSL : na, "Active SL", color=colShort, style=plot.style_linebr, linewidth=2)
plot(inPos ? pendTP1 : na, "Active TP1", color=color.new(colLong, 45), style=plot.style_linebr, linewidth=1)
plot(inPos ? pendTP2 : na, "Active TP2", color=colLong, style=plot.style_linebr, linewidth=2)

// Entry markers, independent of the label setting.
plotshape(longSignal, title="Long signal", style=shape.triangleup, location=location.belowbar, color=colLong, size=size.tiny)
plotshape(shortSignal, title="Short signal", style=shape.triangledown, location=location.abovebar, color=colShort, size=size.tiny)

// ------------------------------------------------------------- status panel

// Declared at global scope: a `var` inside an if-block initialises on the first
// bar the branch runs, which is fragile. This is created once, always.
var table t = table.new(position.top_right, 2, 21, border_width=1, frame_width=1, frame_color=color.gray)

if showTable and barstate.islast
    wins   = strategy.wintrades
    losses = strategy.losstrades
    dec    = wins + losses
    wr     = dec > 0 ? wins / dec * 100.0 : 0.0
    pf     = strategy.grossloss > 0 ? strategy.grossprofit / strategy.grossloss : 0.0
    blocked = not flat ? "in position" :
              targetMet ? "target met -- done" :
              lossCapHit ? "LOSS CAP -- done" :
              tradeCapHit ? "trade cap -- done" :
              lossStreakHit ? "2 losses -- done" :
              coolOffActive ? "cool-off active" : "ready"

    table.cell(t, 0, 0, "XAU Agent v5", text_color=color.white, bgcolor=color.new(color.blue, 30), text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(t, 1, 0, timeframe.period + " / bias " + biasTF, text_color=color.white, bgcolor=color.new(color.blue, 30), text_size=size.small)

    table.cell(t, 0, 1, "bias",  text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(t, 1, 1, bias == 1 ? "BULL" : bias == -1 ? "BEAR" : "none", text_color = bias == 1 ? colLong : bias == -1 ? colShort : color.gray, text_size=size.small)

    table.cell(t, 0, 2, "status", text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(t, 1, 2, blocked, text_color = blocked == "ready" ? colLong : colShort, text_size=size.small)

    table.cell(t, 0, 3, "long score",  text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(t, 1, 3, str.tostring(longScore) + "/" + str.tostring(minScore), text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(t, 0, 4, "short score", text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(t, 1, 4, str.tostring(shortScore) + "/" + str.tostring(minScore), text_size=size.small)

    table.cell(t, 0, 5, "demand zone", text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(t, 1, 5, na(dBot) ? "none" : str.tostring(dBot, format.mintick) + "-" + str.tostring(dTop, format.mintick), text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(t, 0, 6, "supply zone", text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(t, 1, 6, na(sTop) ? "none" : str.tostring(sBot, format.mintick) + "-" + str.tostring(sTop, format.mintick), text_size=size.small)

    table.cell(t, 0, 7, "day P&L", text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(t, 1, 7, "$" + str.tostring(dayPnl, "#.##") + " / " + str.tostring(dailyTarget, "#"), text_color = dayPnl >= 0 ? colLong : colShort, text_size=size.small)

    table.cell(t, 0, 8, "trades today", text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(t, 1, 8, str.tostring(tradesToday) + "/" + str.tostring(maxTrades), text_size=size.small)

    table.cell(t, 0, 9, "win rate", text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(t, 1, 9, str.tostring(wr, "#.#") + "% (" + str.tostring(dec) + " trades)", text_size=size.small)

    table.cell(t, 0, 10, "profit factor", text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(t, 1, 10, str.tostring(pf, "#.##"), text_size=size.small)

    table.cell(t, 0, 11, "volatility", text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(t, 1, 11, na(volMult) ? "warming up" : str.tostring(volMult, "#.##") + "x (" + str.tostring(minVolMult, "#.##") + "-" + str.tostring(maxVolMult, "#.##") + ")", text_color = volOK ? colLong : colShort, text_size=size.small)

    // Why no trade fired: each confirmed bar counted against the FIRST gate it
    // failed. The largest number is the binding constraint.
    table.cell(t, 0, 12, "WHY NO TRADE", text_color=color.white, bgcolor=color.new(color.gray, 40), text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(t, 1, 12, str.tostring(nBars) + " bars", text_color=color.white, bgcolor=color.new(color.gray, 40), text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(t, 0, 13, "no 4h bias",       text_size=size.tiny)
    table.cell(t, 1, 13, f_pct(nBias),       text_size=size.tiny)
    table.cell(t, 0, 14, "no zone",          text_size=size.tiny)
    table.cell(t, 1, 14, f_pct(nZone),       text_size=size.tiny)
    table.cell(t, 0, 15, "zone wrong side",  text_size=size.tiny)
    table.cell(t, 1, 15, f_pct(nSide),       text_size=size.tiny)
    table.cell(t, 0, 16, "zone not tapped",  text_size=size.tiny)
    table.cell(t, 1, 16, f_pct(nTap),        text_size=size.tiny)
    table.cell(t, 0, 17, "no HA trigger",    text_size=size.tiny)
    table.cell(t, 1, 17, f_pct(nHA),         text_size=size.tiny)
    table.cell(t, 0, 18, "volatility gate",  text_size=size.tiny)
    table.cell(t, 1, 18, f_pct(nVol), text_color = nVol > nBars / 2 ? colShort : color.gray, text_size=size.tiny)
    table.cell(t, 0, 19, "score below min",  text_size=size.tiny)
    table.cell(t, 1, 19, f_pct(nScore),      text_size=size.tiny)
    table.cell(t, 0, 20, "risk rules / fired", text_size=size.tiny)
    table.cell(t, 1, 20, f_pct(nRisk) + " / " + str.tostring(nFired), text_size=size.tiny)

// ------------------------------------------------------------- alerts
// Create these in TradingView: right-click chart -> Add alert -> Condition =
// this script. Use "Once per bar close" so it matches the tested behaviour.

alertcondition(longSignal, title="XAU long entry", message="XAUUSD LONG {{ticker}} @ {{close}} -- see chart for SL/TP")
alertcondition(shortSignal, title="XAU short entry", message="XAUUSD SHORT {{ticker}} @ {{close}} -- see chart for SL/TP")

if longSignal
    alert("XAUUSD LONG @ " + str.tostring(longEntry, format.mintick) + " SL " + str.tostring(longSL, format.mintick) + " TP1 " + str.tostring(longTP1, format.mintick) + " TP2 " + str.tostring(longTP2, format.mintick) + " score " + str.tostring(longScore) + "/100" + " size " + str.tostring(longQty) + " oz", alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if shortSignal
    alert("XAUUSD SHORT @ " + str.tostring(shortEntry, format.mintick) + " SL " + str.tostring(shortSL, format.mintick) + " TP1 " + str.tostring(shortTP1, format.mintick) + " TP2 " + str.tostring(shortTP2, format.mintick) + " score " + str.tostring(shortScore) + "/100" + " size " + str.tostring(shortQty) + " oz", alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
